**Issue**: #115
**Date**: 2026-09-22
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Detect decimal digits in a completed greeting
  @SCN001
  Scenario: Detect ASCII and Unicode decimal digits
    Given the installed greeting library
    When greeting_has_digit is called for Ada7, Ada٣, and Ada
    Then it returns True, True, and False respectively

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Reject invalid names with existing validation
    Given blank, whitespace-only, and non-string names
    When greeting_has_digit is called
    Then the existing greet ValueError is raised

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve existing greeting and CLI output
    Given the installed package
    When greet and nmg-smoke greet Ada
    Then the existing Hello, Ada output and CLI newline are unchanged
    And all existing public exports remain available
